-- title:
--   No cusp-free smooth-point package at an end (q=2)
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q=2$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $\ell$ is a prime with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Further, $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}=$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a non-unit of $A$ (`A.LiesOverPrime q`), with residue field $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`. Two function fields occur: `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, the $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series generated by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field, and `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, the corresponding base change of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_H(q^2M')$, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$; `hle` asserts the inclusion of the first field in the second. A finset $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ is given, with `hW` saying that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' κ`, i.e. the places $w$ that are rational, satisfy the predicate `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and have $w$-value of the generator `jGeomGen κ M'` in the set `ssJSet q κ`; $s$ is an element of $W$. Moreover $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` — a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective residue map onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places of the right degree, compatibility with $A$ and with the residue map of $A$, and the existence for each nonzero $f$ of a scalar $c$ with $c f$ integral of nonzero residue; `hR₀` states that $R_0$ is computed coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-Laurent series lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its residue, viewed as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $\pi\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfies $\pi^{q^2-1}=q$ and $\pi\in A$.
--
--   On the reduction side, $F_{ss}$ is a field over $\kappa$, $R$ is a `RegularProlongation` of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $F_{ss}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with surjective residue map onto $F_{ss}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$, and with the scaling property above), $N$ is a finset of places of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$, and, indexed by places $Q$ of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$, there are data $S_Q$ (a subring of `fieldBar q M'`), $\varphi_Q:A[T]\to S_Q$, $\chi_{0,Q}:S_Q\to\kappa$ and $D_Q$ (a set of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$). Write $j$ for the element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` given by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion `jq` of the modular invariant, and also for its image in `fieldBar q M'` under `IntermediateField.inclusion hle`.
--
--   The hypotheses on these data are: `h0`, that $F_{ss}$ contains an element transcendental over $\kappa$; `h1`, that $R$ lies over $s$, namely for every $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ whose order is $\ge 0$ at every place of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` at which the order of $j$ is $\ge 0$, and whose $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue is the image in $F_{ss}$ of the value of the $R_0$-residue of $f$ at $s$; `h2`, that $R.\mathrm{integers}$ is invariant under all the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` for $\zeta$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ (an element of `Idx q`) and $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$; and `hcard`, that $N$ has exactly $q+1$ elements.
--
--   The hypothesis `hpkg` asserts that for every place $Q\notin N$ the quadruple $(S_Q,\varphi_Q,\chi_{0,Q},D_Q)$ is a smooth-point package, i.e. the conjunction of the following fourteen clauses: (i) $S_Q$ contains the image of $A$ under the structure map $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`; (ii) $\varphi_Q$ is formally smooth; (iii) $\varphi_Q$ is formally unramified; (iv) $\varphi_Q(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$ for every $a\in A$; (v) $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ for every $a\in A$; (vi) $\chi_{0,Q}(\varphi_Q(X))=0$; (vii) for every $c\in A$ with residue $0$ there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi:S_Q\to A$ with $\chi(\varphi_Q(C\,a))=a$ for all $a\in A$, with residue of $\chi(f)$ equal to $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$ for all $f$, and with $\chi(\varphi_Q(X))=c$; (viii) every $f\in S_Q$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, its $R$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $Q$, and the residue there of that element is the image of $\chi_{0,Q}(f)$ in the residue field of $Q$; (ix) $\varphi_Q(X)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R$-residue has $Q$-order $1$; (x) a place $P$ belongs to $D_Q$ exactly when $P$ is rational, every $f\in S_Q$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P$-value in $A$, and for every $f\in S_Q$ the $A$-valuation of that value is $<1$ precisely when $\chi_{0,Q}(f)=0$; (xi) for every ring homomorphism $\chi:S_Q\to A$ splitting $\varphi_Q\circ C$ and reducing to $\chi_{0,Q}$ there is a unique $P\in D_Q$ with $P$-value of $f$ equal to $\chi(f)$ for all $f\in S_Q$; (xii) for $P\in D_Q$, an element $f$ of `fieldBar q M'` lies in the valuation subring of $P$ exactly when $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in S_Q$ with $P$-value of $h$ nonzero; (xiii) every nonzero $f$ with $P$-order $0$ for all $P\in D_Q$ becomes a unit of $S_Q$ after multiplication by the image of a nonzero scalar $c\in\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$; (xiv) every $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ lying in the valuation subring of every $P\in D_Q$ lies in $S_Q$. The hypothesis `hdisj` states that these discs are pairwise disjoint: for $Q,Q'\notin N$, if some $P$ lies in $D_Q$ and in $D_{Q'}$, then $Q=Q'$. The hypothesis `hcusp` states cusp-freeness of the discs: for $Q\notin N$ and $P\in D_Q$, the $P$-order of $j$ is $\ge 0$. The hypothesis `heqv` states equivariance: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, and every proof that $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced automorphism `R.resAut` of $F_{ss}$ permutes $N$ (membership in $N$ is preserved and reflected), and for $Q\notin N$ the translate `smulDisc τ (Dx Q)` is $D_{\,\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q}$.
--
--   The hypothesis `hK` is a single large existential statement asserting the existence of annuli and node presentations at the ends; its clauses are grouped as follows, and are summarised here. There is an assignment $x\mapsto An_x$ of an `Annulus` of $A$ in `fieldBar q M'` to each place of $F_{ss}$ over $\kappa$ such that: for $x\in N$, the parameter of $An_x$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R$-residue of $x$-order $1$ and satisfies the slope-unit property (for $f\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue and order $0$ on the domain of $An_x$, at each $P$ of that domain the product of the $P$-value of $f$ with the $(-x\text{-order of the residue})$-th power of the $P$-value of the parameter is a unit of $A$), the modulus of $An_x$ is nonzero, the domain of $An_x$ meets no disc $D_Q$ with $Q\notin N$, and every $P$ in the domain is near $s$ (for $f\in R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ subject to the order condition against $j$ and with $R_0$-residue in the valuation subring of $s$, and for $a\in A$ whose residue is the value at $s$ of that $R_0$-residue, the $P$-value of the image of $f$ differs from $a$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$); the domains of $An_x$, $x\in N$, are pairwise disjoint; these domains are permuted by the level automorphisms compatibly with `R.resAut`; every rational place $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ that is near $s$ in the above sense lies in some $D_Q$ with $Q\notin N$ or in some domain $An_x$ with $x\in N$; for distinct $x,x'\in N$ there is $g\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue, nonzero $x$-order of that residue, $P$-order $0$ on the domain of $An_x$, and $P$-value a unit of $A$ on the domain of $An_{x'}$. Finally `hK` provides the node presentations: fields $F_{I,x}$ over $\kappa$ with regular prolongations $R_x$ of $A$ to `fieldBar q M'` and places $b_x$ of $F_{I,x}$; an index type $\Lambda$ with discrete valuation subrings $C'_l\subseteq A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with uniformisers $\varpi'_l$ and a base index $l_0$; complete discrete valuation rings $W_l$ with uniformisers $\pi_{W,l}$, exponents $E_l\ge 1$ and $E_0$; sets of places $S_{nd}$, subrings $\mathcal{N}_{nd}$ and local Noetherian subrings $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$, and elements $c_{x},c_{y},c_{u}$; together with clauses stating: the residue criterion characterising divisibility by $\varpi'_l$, monotonicity $C'_{l_0}\le C'_l$, nonvanishing of $\varpi'_{l_0}$, algebraicity of $A$ over $C'_{l_0}$, irreducibility of $\pi_{W,l}$, invariance of $\varpi'_{l_0}$ under the elements of the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ on which the tame character at $\pi$ is trivial, and a relation $\varpi'^{\,E_0}_{l_0}=v\,\pi^{w}$ with $v$ a unit of $A$ and $w\ge 1$; and, for each $nd\in N$: rationality of $b_{nd}$, of $nd$ and of the places in $S_{nd}$, the description of $\mathcal{N}_{nd}$ as the elements integral for $R_{nd}$, for $R$ and at every $P\in S_{nd}$, integrality of their values at those places, the crossing relation $c_x c_y=\varpi'^{\,E_0}_{l_0}c_u$ with the four prescribed residue and order conditions on $c_x$ and $c_y$ relative to $R$, $R_{nd}$, $nd$ and $b_{nd}$, invariance of $S_{nd}$, $c_x$ and $c_y$ under the arithmetic Galois action of tame-trivial inertia elements through [`ModularCurve.arithmeticGalois`](def/ModularCurve_ArithmeticGalois.html#L54) on `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, generation of `fieldBar q M'` as a field of fractions of the $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ and as a $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-span over $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l_0}$, and for each $l$ the chain $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l_0}\le\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}\le\mathcal{N}_{nd}$, the characterisation of $S_{nd}$ by integrality and specialisation of non-units of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$, the inclusion of $C'_l$, approximation of elements of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ by elements of $C'_l$ up to non-units, a $C'_l$-linear independence clause, the existence of a subring $B$ generated over $C'_l$ by finitely many elements, containing $c_x,c_y,c_u$, with $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ its localisation, membership and unit properties of $c_x,c_y,c_u$, and an isomorphism of the adic completion of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ with `UVCrossingModel (Wc l) (πW l ^ E l)` together with a map $\sigma$ from $W_l$ sending $\pi_{W,l}$ to $\varpi'_l$, matching constants, hitting $C'_l$, and carrying an element of $\mathcal{N}_{0,nd,l}$ whose $R_{nd}$-residue has $b_{nd}$-order $n$ (respectively whose $R$-residue has $nd$-order $n$) to a unit multiple of $V^n$ modulo $(\pi_{W,l},U)$ (respectively of $U^n$ modulo $(\pi_{W,l},V)$). A further clause supplies the Hasse datum on $j$: `jqNModC` of level $q$ lies in `fieldBar q M'`, and there are $a_0\in A$ with $J-a_0\in R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $R$-residue $0$, with the residue of $a_0$ raised to the $q$-th power equal to the value at $s$ of `jGeomGen κ M'`, and a scalar $c'$ such that $c'(J-a_0)$ has nonzero $R$-residue and for every $nd\in N$ the element $J-a_0$ lies in $R_{nd}.\mathrm{integers}$ with nonzero residue and $nd$-order of the $R$-residue of $c'(J-a_0)$ equal to minus the $b_{nd}$-order of the $R_{nd}$-residue of $J-a_0$. The remaining clauses state that the sets $S_{nd}$ are pairwise disjoint, that every $P\in S_{nd}$ is near $s$ in the above sense, that the level automorphisms permute $N$ compatibly with $S$ and with the rings $R_{nd}.\mathrm{integers}$ and that the subgroup they generate permutes $N$ and the sets $S_{nd}$ through `R.resAut`, that $S_{nd}$ is the domain of $An_{nd}$ for $nd\in N$, that $R_0$-integral elements are $R_{nd}$-integral, and that for each $nd\in N$ there is a ring homomorphism $j_{nd}$ from `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` to $F_{I,nd}$ computing the $R_{nd}$-residues of $R_0$-integral elements and satisfying that $g$ lies in the valuation subring of $s$ exactly when $j_{nd}(g)$ lies in that of $b_{nd}$.
--
--   Under all these hypotheses the conclusion is: for every place $Q\in N$, every subring $S$ of `fieldBar q M'`, every ring homomorphism $\varphi:A[T]\to S$, every ring homomorphism $\chi_0:S\to\kappa$ and every set $D$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, the conjunction of the fourteen clauses (i)–(xiv) above, read with this $Q\in N$ and with $(S,\varphi,\chi_0,D)$ in place of $(S_Q,\varphi_Q,\chi_{0,Q},D_Q)$, together with the cusp-free clause that the $P$-order of $j$ is $\ge 0$ for every $P\in D$, is false. In other words, no place of $N$ carries a cusp-free smooth-point package.
--
--   The statement is the step, in the analysis of the stable reduction of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ at $q$, which shows that the $q+1$ places singled out as the ends of the supersingular component are genuine ends: none of them admits an étale chart with a cusp-free residue disc. It is the case $q=2$, at an auxiliary rigid level given by a prime $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, of the corresponding statement for larger $q$, and it is used in assembling the full package of regular prolongations, smooth-point charts, node presentations and the Igusa datum on the special fibre.
